  "_comment": [
    "SYNTHETIC — hand-built from the documented response shapes in Yahoo's official",
    "Fantasy Sports API guide and from published wrapper-library samples (yfpy,",
    "yahoo_fantasy_api). NOT a live capture. Yahoo API access is gated behind an",
    "approval application and NO live call has ever been made from this repo.",
    "Replace with a real redacted capture once API access is approved.",
    "",
    "AUTHORED 2026-08-11 (not captured on any date).",
    "MODELS: GET /fantasy/v2/league/461.l.576919/standings?format=json",
    "        (a FINISHED season — is_finished 1, current_week == end_week)",
    "",
    "REDACTION: all identifiers invented — team keys, team names and manager",
    "GUIDs (FAKEGUID...) are fake.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS IS COMMITTED — THE LEADING DOT. Team t.6 has an outcome percentage",
    "of \".571\". Not \"0.571\". Yahoo strips the leading zero, and that single",
    "character is a parser-breaker: JavaScript's parseInt('.571') is NaN,",
    "int('.571') raises, and a Number-vs-null coalesce turns it into 0 — a team",
    "that went 8-6 recorded as having won nothing. to_float() handles it, and",
    "this fixture is the only thing that proves it still does.",
    "",
    "SECOND VALUE THAT BREAKS NAIVE PARSING: games_back is the literal string",
    "'-' for the first-place team. Not 0, not empty, not null — a dash. to_float()",
    "returns None for it, which is right: the leader is not zero games back in the",
    "same sense that a 2.0 is a number; Yahoo is drawing a table, not reporting a",
    "measurement. Anything that coerces '-' to 0 will look correct and be wrong.",
    "",
    "THIRD THING THIS FILE ENCODES — a limit, not a feature. ⚠️ THIS IS THE ONLY",
    "STANDINGS STATE YAHOO WILL EVER GIVE YOU. There is no standings;week=N. For a",
    "completed season you get the final table and nothing else; for a live one you",
    "get today's. Every intermediate week has to be RECONSTRUCTED from the",
    "scoreboards, and every reconstructed row is written with is_inferred=1 and a",
    "basis. The rows parsed from this payload are the only ones entitled to",
    "is_inferred=0.",
    "",
    "SHAPE HAZARDS DELIBERATELY PRESENT:",
    "  1. 'standings' is a one-element ARRAY wrapping the teams collection —",
    "     [ {\"teams\": {...}} ] — while 'teams' inside it is a numeric-key",
    "     COLLECTION with a sibling 'count'. Two different container conventions,",
    "     one nested inside the other, in the same payload.",
    "  2. 'team' is an ARRAY whose element 0 is an ARRAY of single-key dicts.",
    "  3. wins/losses arrive as bare INTs on some teams and STRINGS on others.",
    "  4. A team with a TIE is present (t.9, 7-6-1). Ties are rare enough that",
    "     code paths silently assume wins+losses == games played.",
    "  5. points_for appears BOTH as team_standings.points_for AND as",
    "     team_points.total on t.4 only. The parser prefers team_standings and",
    "     falls back — and the two agree here, deliberately, so the fallback can",
    "     be tested without also testing a disagreement.",
    "  6. clinched_playoffs is present on the top four teams and ABSENT on the",
    "     rest. Absent is not 0 — for an eliminated team Yahoo simply stops",
    "     mentioning it.",
    "  7. streak is a sub-object {type, value}; 'value' is a string.",
    "",
    "TRUNCATED to 6 of 12 teams. Reason: the remaining six are the same code path",
    "and would add 300 lines. The six kept cover: the leader (games_back '-',",
    "clinched), the leading-dot percentage, a tie record, a losing streak, both",
    "divisions, and a team with no clinched_playoffs key at all."
  ],
